<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
		<Title>TestFramework.Container.Web</Title>
		<Version>0.2.1</Version>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<Description>Docker-backed environment providers for TestFramework.Web timelines: builds and runs the application under test, starts the SQL Server behind it and the stubbed dependencies in front of it, and publishes every address into the running timeline.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Container</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Container.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Timeline;Docker;Web;Sql;SqlServer</PackageTags>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Rebuilt on TestFramework.Container 0.1.1, which is where the change is.
Changed in 0.1.1:
- Building an image from a project no longer depends on the registry being reachable, and no longer rebuilds the same image for every environment. A suite of a dozen chapters against one unchanged application used to pay for a dozen identical publishes; it now pays for one. Measured on a web suite: 25 minutes down to under 3.
- An image the Docker daemon cannot pull is fetched by the test process over IPv4 and loaded in, so a broken IPv6 path to a registry no longer stops a run on a machine nobody is allowed to reconfigure.
- Every dotnet invocation is bounded and killed with its process tree, so a wedged publish cannot hang a run or outlive it.
Previously: Initial release: container-backed SQL Server, application and stubbed dependencies for web timelines.
Worth knowing up front:
- A container reused across runs keeps whatever the previous run wrote, so SqlResetMode decides what happens to the database between runs - recreate it, run a reset script, or leave it alone.
- Published ports bind to 127.0.0.1 rather than every interface, and the SQL Server password is generated per environment instead of being a constant shipped in the package. Use UseSqlPassword(...) to pin it, which a reused container needs.
- Where the application under test comes from is declared rather than guessed, through the same ContainerSource model as TestFramework.Container: an image, a project path, or a directory. The resolved plan is logged before anything is built.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Container.Web.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Container is consumed as a published package, not as a project, so the dependency this
		     package declares is exactly the one a consumer resolves. Container must be published
		     before this package ships against it. -->
		<PackageReference Include="TestFramework.Container" Version="0.2.1" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="6.1.2" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="10.0.0" />
		<!-- Direct reference overrides the vulnerable SSH.NET 2025.1.0 that Testcontainers pulls in
		     transitively (GHSA-q939-rpr3-3284). Testcontainers still pins it as of 4.13.0. -->
		<PackageReference Include="SSH.NET" Version="2026.0.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Testcontainers" Version="4.11.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Testcontainers.MsSql" Version="4.11.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="TestFramework.Config" Version="0.2.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="TestFramework.Core" Version="0.3.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="TestFramework.Web" Version="0.3.0" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
